From 86481e9f50ba593a96325ef22dfb483f56a9bfb7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andy1210 <andy1210@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 06:08:08 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 062/137] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8350: Add the camera subsystem

Describe CAMSS (Titan 580) with the addresses and interrupts of the
vendor device tree: six CSIPHYs (the fifth on GIC SPI 122, not 86 as on
SM8250), three full IFEs with their CSIDs (the third at 0xacef000, SPI
640/641) and two lite ones, the IFE stream IDs of the vendor camera
SMMU node, the SM8250 interconnect paths and the IFE0/1/2 and Titan top
GDSCs. Add the qcom,sm8350-camss binding.

Depends on "media: qcom: camss: Add SM8350 support" and the SM8350
camera clock controller.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 .../bindings/media/qcom,sm8350-camss.yaml     | 331 ++++++++++++++++++
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8350.dtsi          | 199 +++++++++++
 2 files changed, 530 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/qcom,sm8350-camss.yaml

